  "status_text": "Covering the ones in a grid with rectangles can decide how many wires a circuit needs to carry groups of words. Lean checked a construction from any grid of zeros and ones (L-lib-1438). It gives separate groups of words. The decoder must return each encoded word to its original group. Both maps use only functions that never turn an output off when inputs turn on. They meet the specified width limit exactly when the grid's ones can be covered by at most the chosen number of all-one rectangles. Each rectangle may use any rows and columns.",
